{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. You’re here because of vomiting, high blood sugar, and feeling very weak. We’ve started you on fluids and insulin through your IV. How are you feeling right now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better since the fluids, but I was so sick earlier. My mouth was so dry, and I couldn’t keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your blood sugar was extremely high—over 1000. That’s what caused the diabetic ketoacidosis, or DKA. We’re treating it with insulin and fluids. We also placed a central line in your neck because your veins were hard to access."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that thing in my neck? I felt them working on me but I was so out of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s the central line. It helps us give you medications and fluids more easily. Your labs also showed very high potassium, which can be dangerous for the heart. We’ve treated that, and your EKG is looking better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "High potassium? But I thought I was low on everything. I haven’t been eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good point. Even though your blood showed high potassium, your body is actually depleted overall. As we correct the DKA, the potassium will shift, so we’re watching it closely and replacing it safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I skipped my Lantus for a couple days because I was nauseous and didn’t feel like eating. I thought maybe I didn’t need it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely what triggered the DKA. Even when you’re not eating, your body still needs background insulin. Skipping it, especially with type 1 diabetes, can lead to this. We’ll help you adjust your doses before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know, I know. I’ve been trying. I haven’t had alcohol for a month now. I’m really trying to stay on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ve started you on vitamins, including thiamine, just to support you. We’re also monitoring for any signs of withdrawal, but so far you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. And my kidneys—are they okay? Last time I was here, they were affected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine was elevated to 1.9, but your baseline is around 0.6. This is due to severe dehydration from DKA. With fluids, it’s already improving. We expect it to return to normal, just like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my old abscess site—is it infected again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, the site is healed and there’s no sign of infection. We checked your urine, blood, and chest X-ray—all clear. No source of infection this time. This DKA seems related to missed insulin, not an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2161-04-11 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief. I was worried it came back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2161-04-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee again. Your labs from this morning show improvement. Your blood sugar is down to 250, and your anion gap is closing. We’re transitioning you from the insulin drip to subcutaneous insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2161-04-12 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Does that mean I can eat?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2161-04-12 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start you on a light diet. But we know you have gastroparesis, so we’ll go slow. Small, frequent meals. The nurse will help you time your insulin with meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2161-04-12 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hate that my stomach empties so slowly. Makes it hard to manage insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2161-04-12 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll work with the diabetes educator to help you adjust. Also, your white blood cell count was high when you came in—15.1—but that’s common in DKA as a stress response. It’s already coming down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2161-04-12 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I heard my count dropped later? I overheard a nurse say I was neutropenic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2161-04-12 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your WBC dropped to 2.9 yesterday evening, with low neutrophils. We don’t know why, but this pattern happened last time too. No fever or infection, so we’re watching it. It’s likely related to your diabetes fluctuations."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2161-04-12 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it dangerous? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2161-04-12 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right now, you’re not at risk because you have no fever or infection. We put you on neutropenic precautions—meaning we’re extra careful with hygiene. Your count is expected to rebound, as it did last admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2161-04-12 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief. I’ll need to follow up on that, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2161-04-12 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we recommend an outpatient evaluation to understand why this keeps happening. But for now, your main issue was DKA, and you’re recovering well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2161-04-13 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning show your kidney function has normalized—creatinine is 0.7. Potassium is stable at 4.1. You’re off the insulin drip and doing well on injections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2161-04-13 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. I’ve been checking my sugars every few hours like they taught me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2161-04-13 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. But we noticed a few lows—like 60 this morning. That’s why we’re reducing your Lantus dose from 12 units to 10 in the morning and 5 at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2161-04-13 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t realize I was that low. I just felt shaky."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2161-04-13 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, hypoglycemia can be dangerous. We want to avoid that. The diabetes educator will review your sliding scale and meal timing before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2161-04-13 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll pay more attention. I don’t want to end up back here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2161-04-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white count is now 2.9, but neutrophils are up to 35%. You’re no longer neutropenic. It’s improving, just like we expected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2161-04-14 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s rebounding? That’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2161-04-14 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. It’s a strange pattern, but consistent with your history. Still, we recommend seeing a specialist to look into it further."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2161-04-14 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make the appointment. I’ve got my primary care next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2161-04-15 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. Your blood sugar is stable, kidneys are normal, and your CBC is improving. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2161-04-15 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about support at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2161-04-15 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll have a visiting nurse coming daily to help with glucose checks, insulin, and making sure you’re taking all your meds. We’re also assigning a case manager through your insurance to help coordinate services."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2161-04-15 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I live alone, so it helps to know someone’s checking in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2161-04-15 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know you’re at high risk for readmission, so we want to give you every support. Keep your follow-up with endocrinology and your PCP. And please call if your sugars are high or low for more than a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2161-04-15 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And no alcohol—I’m sticking to that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2161-04-15 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We’ll keep you on your depression meds—mirtazapine and Effexor. How’s your mood been?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2161-04-15 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I’ve been talking to my mom more. She’s proud I’ve been sober."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2161-04-15 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. Support from family makes a big difference. We’ll see you one last time tomorrow before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2161-04-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your final labs are excellent—normal kidney function, stable CBC, blood sugar 143. You’re ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2161-04-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel so much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2161-04-16 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made great progress. Remember: take your insulin even when you’re not feeling well, watch for lows, and keep your appointments. The nurse will be by this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2161-04-16 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll call if anything’s wrong. Thank you, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2161-04-16 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we hope not to see you back here soon. Stay healthy."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2161-04-11 20:56:00",
